<title>DENMARK: FORECAST - Paribas ups Danish 97 GDP growth estimate.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Paribas ups Danish 97 GDP growth estimate.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>In its latest survey France's Paribas Capital Markets on Monday raised its expectations for Denmark's 1997 GDP (gross domestic product) growth to 3.3 percent from 2.7 percent in its last forecast in December 1996.</p>
<p>At the same time it upped its Danish inflation forecast for this year to 2.8 percent from 2.7 percent.</p>
<p>The latest Danish Economy Ministry forecast in December foresaw 2.9 percent GDP growth, 2.3 percent inflation, 8.0 percent unemployment and a current account surplus of 13.0 billion crowns for this year.</p>
<p>The following estimates were made by 10 leading local and international organisations.</p>
<p>	  (pct)	 GDP    inflation  unemployment c/a (bln Dkk)</p>
<p>Paribas (3/97)	3.3    2.8	  7.6	   10.2</p>
<p>Sydbank (2/97)	3.0    2.5	  8.0	   12.0</p>
<p>Spar Nord (2/97)    2.5    2.4	  8.0	    5.0</p>
<p>Chase M'hattan(2/97)2.6    2.4	   --	    8.5</p>
<p>Svenska H'bank(2/97)3.5    2.5	  7.8	    0.0</p>
<p>Citibank (2/97)     2.9    2.4	  8.2	   15.0</p>
<p>PaineWebber (2/97)  2.7    2.5	  7.4	    6.3</p>
<p>Nykredit (2/97)     2.3    2.5	  8.4	    8.0</p>
<p>BG Bank (2/97)	3.0    2.5	  7.9	    4.0</p>
<p>NatWest (2/97)	3.0    2.6	  8.2	    8.3</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
</text>
